      "title": "Why Models Hallucinate",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Why Models Hallucinate",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What It Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Hallucination== = fluent output that is **false** or unsupported by the source",
                "Model predicts the {blue:likely next token}, not a verified fact",
                "Cause: {red:gaps or errors} in training data",
                "Cause: {orange:rare, long-tail} facts",
                "Cause: ==knowledge cutoff== (no data after a date)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Two Kinds",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Versus the context",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**Intrinsic**",
                  "Contradicts it",
                  "Source says 2019, answer says 2021"
                ],
                [
                  "**Extrinsic**",
                  "Adds claims it cannot verify",
                  "Invents a quote not in the source"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Why It Persists",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Training rewards ==confident guessing== over \"I don't know\"",
                "Models abstain **too rarely**",
                "Allow a {green:'not found'} answer and instruct it: abstaining becomes far likelier"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Common Mistake",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Low temperature is not truth",
              "text": "Temperature 0 makes decoding greedy: it picks the ==likeliest token==, not a verified fact."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Grounding and Citations",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Grounding and Citations",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Grounding Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Grounding== = answers rest on **supplied sources**, not model memory",
                "Sources: {blue:RAG chunks}, {purple:tool/API results}, {orange:database lookups}"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Workflow and Citations",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Retrieve",
                    "sub": "top-k chunks",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Prompt",
                    "sub": "chunks as context",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Instruct",
                    "sub": "answer only from the context",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Fallback",
                    "sub": "else say 'not found'",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Citation== = tag each claim with a **source ID** or chunk quote",
                "A reader or a program can then verify the claim"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Verify Citations",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Check the cited ==ID exists== in the retrieved set",
                "Check the ==quoted span appears== in that source",
                "Reject any claim that fails either check"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "python",
              "lines": [
                "def verify(cite, sources):",
                "    text = sources.get(cite[\"id\"])",
                "    return text is not None and cite[\"quote\"] in text"
              ],
              "note": "missing ID or missing quote means reject"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "A citation proves nothing alone",
              "text": "Models can cite **real** sources that do not support the claim. Bad retrieval gives ==confident wrong== answers."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Evaluation Methods",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Evaluation Methods",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three Ways to Score",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Method",
                "Good for",
                "Catch"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Benchmark",
                  "cheap, reproducible, comparable",
                  "contamination; may not match your task"
                ],
                [
                  "LLM-as-judge",
                  "scales cheaply, rubric scoring",
                  "position, verbosity, self-preference bias"
                ],
                [
                  "Human eval",
                  "==gold standard== for nuance, safety",
                  "slow, costly"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Classic {red:MMLU, HumanEval, GSM8K} are ==saturated== at ~90%+",
                "{orange:MMLU-Pro, GPQA Diamond} are nearing saturation too",
                "Separate current models with ==Humanity's Last Exam==, ==SWE-bench Pro=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Golden Set and Agreement",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Golden set",
                    "sub": "50-200 real examples",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Expected answers",
                    "sub": "per example",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Run",
                    "sub": "every prompt or model change",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Measure inter-annotator agreement: ==Cohen's kappa=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Relying on public benchmark rank alone",
                "Trusting an unvalidated judge"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Calibrate the judge",
              "text": "Compare judge scores with ==human labels==, and **swap answer order** to cancel position bias."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
